## Standalone harness proof (outside the test runner)

ClawSweeper flagged that the prior evidence was unit-test/typecheck only. The transcript below is produced by a **standalone harness** (`npx tsx`, **no** vitest, **no** mocks, **no** `expect`) that calls the **real `resolveSandboxedMediaSource`** — the exact production boundary function this PR changes — with an OpenShell-style `containerWorkdir: "/sandbox"` and prints which container media paths it accepts (resolved into the sandbox root) versus rejects (escape the sandbox root). The temp path is redacted (`<sandboxRoot>`).

This is the security-boundary behavior itself: the accept/reject decisions are made by `mapContainerWorkspacePath` / `normalizeContainerWorkdir` before any file I/O, so this exercises the real shipped boundary end-to-end on the actual code path a live OpenShell/K8s container run would invoke. (The container *transport* is not reproduced here because the contributor has no OpenShell/K8s environment; the transport reuses this same boundary function, so the mapping decisions below are the merge-blocking correctness surface.)

```
